WEBVTT

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.080
Ray!

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.700
Are you all right?

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.330
Force Heal!

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.250
Anyone with extra MP, use it to heal this fellow
and any other injured persons!

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.250
All others, come with me to save Her Highness!

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.160
Roger that!

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:37.910
I can restore his HP...
but I'm unable to heal his Charred arm.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.120
Just keep him alive for now.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.580
I'm sure he doesn't want to back out now.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.250
Congratulations are in order!

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:55.790
We are now 251 seconds past the
original monster-release deadline.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:00.660
And, oh, dear--it looks like
my remote is indeed broken!

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.580
My modded monsters never did get unleashed.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:10.370
Aaand here's my <i>spare</i> remote!

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.700
Why, you...

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.700
I always make a spare
in case the first one breaks.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.200
But see, this one doesn't have a timer.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.500
So I'm just gonna press it!

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.040
Boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop...

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.040
Franklin!

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.370
Your battle was highly entertaining!

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:33.410
Can't say I was a fan of the ending, though.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.080
Please take over Ray's treatment.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:43.450
What's this? Is Miss Vice-Captain off
to give aid, beat-up as she is?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.450
Or does she mean to defeat me?

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.870
What a go-getter! But it'll never work.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:54.540
Call: DGP, KOS!

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.620
Those are--

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.040
Turns out the RSK was
the <i>weakest</i> pawn in my game.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.870
<i>These</i> babies have the battle
strength of a Legendary UBM.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:21.330
I used that RSK because Ray took down
those Demi-Drag-class Worms.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:27.450
I figured I'd try again with
a Pure-Dragon-tier beastie.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.540
Then he went and beat me again.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.700
That's right: I'm 0 for 2 against Ray.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.500
I <i>will</i> repay this debt
<i>and</i> my humiliation in full.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.950
Still, I have no intention
of tonight's plan failing.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.700
Now, let's see how the city's doing, shall we?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.370
Huh? They haven't been released?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:03:00.370
The remote's working fine.
An issue on the other end, then.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:04.660
But you'd need some major Conceal skills to--

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.370
The Superior Killer.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.040
Good thing I made it in time!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.500
My Conceal Sense is top-notch--

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.080
you can't hide anything from <i>me</i> .

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.450
Hilarious!

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:26.040
Wow, everybody and her brother is dead set
on ripping my plans to shreds, huh?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.160
So that's that.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.620
No--it's not over yet.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.950
What?

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.620
Franklin's not about to let it end here.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.620
His Plan A and Plan B were both crushed.
He's out of options.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.950
Do you really believe that?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:46.700
Yes. He promised me he'd keep
tian casualties to a minimum.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.700
You see Franklin through clouded eyes.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.200
Are you saying I'm blind?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.700
Yes. From where I stand,
he's perfectly capable of slaughter.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.910
Impossible. He's just like me!

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:07.540
He'd <i>never</i> slaughter tians.
He sees them as living, breathing beings!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.620
Which doesn't preclude a massacre.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.000
He just wouldn't do such a thing.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.870
I... I... I've known him for a long time!

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.450
What do <i>you</i> know about him, anyway?

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:25.250
Well... I only know of him through hearsay
and this most recent incident.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.080
I've never even spoken with him directly.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.700
But I can confidently say
my assumptions are correct.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.910
How so?

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:37.080
Precisely because I <i>don't</i> know Franklin.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.700
Taking into account only what he's already done,

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:43.750
he's sure to have something
even more sinister up his sleeve.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.000
Anyone would assume that much.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.660
In fact, you must be the only one who doesn't.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.540
Since you trust Franklin, let me give you
not a deduction, but a prediction.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.370
A prediction?

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.620
Franklin is about to say something horrible.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.410
Well, I sure am in a pickle.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:11.370
Those scary muscleheads'll be emerging
from the arena any minute now.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:16.040
At this point, I have no choice
but to proceed with Plan C.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.750
That's "C" as in "Crisis":

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:27.950
The utter annihilation of Gideon at
the hands of 56,826 modded monsters.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.080
56,826 modded monsters?!

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.020
"Chapter 12: 
King of Destruction"

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:08.910
If only you'd given up sooner--
this would never have happened!

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:13.750
Execute that ruffian before he summons
those monsters from his Jewel!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:17.700
Oh, please! If I had to summon
them each individually,

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.700
I wouldn't even reach
10,000 before daybreak.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.540
Optical Disguise: Cancel!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:51.250
This is my Superior Embryo.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:57.540
Type Plant Fortress:
Magic Beast Factory, Pandemonium!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:10.250
Now... what say we start with
5,000 of my Suicide Series?

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:30.620
Extravagance never felt so good.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.080
Get Franklin. Act now--we can still make it!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.750
I'm afraid that won't work.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.040
These fellas'll keep going even after I'm dead.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.870
Heck, even <i>I</i> can't stop 'em.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.040
These monsters are your doing, aren't they?

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.750
Sure are. I created them with my Pandemonium,

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.790
but they're not mine--not anymore.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.950
Thing is, I let them go.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.790
What are you saying?

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:03.750
You know: Little thing called minion capacity?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.700
I may have a Superior job,
but I can't take in <i>that</i> many beasties.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:13.120
Oh, and don't worry: I properly programmed
them before setting them free.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.830
They won't come near me.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:18.120
They'll keep moving forward until they die,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:25.250
slaughtering everything but my clan members
and the creatures I've created.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.450
And <i>that's</i> why they're the Suicide Series!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:31.750
<i>Tu as compris?</i>

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:37.450
There aren't enough of us here...
We're no match for that many monsters.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.910
It's too la--

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.910
I'll buy us time!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.540
Ray!

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.080
Silver!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.700
Let's go, Nemesis!

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.580
Right!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.540
Brings a tear to my eye, it does!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:12.910
<i>Your</i> battle is over.
You should have kept snoozing.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.370
Not yet.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.750
My battle's <i>far</i> from over.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.120
You can't stop my pace,
my sword-wielding arm--not yet.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:25.620
Not as long as I see tragedy
before me--tragedy and <i>you</i> !

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.700
Liliana! You and your troops handle Pandemonium!

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:37.580
Hell Miasma!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.330
Ray!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.450
Ray!

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.250
I will assist.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:15.790
We are outnumbered.
We must try to work together.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.870
Right. Thanks, Marie.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.910
<i>What</i> ?!

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.830
How did you know?

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.160
I couldn't tell when we first met,

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.660
but now I can see it's you
even through that mist.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.830
Aw, man...

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:40.910
I feel like a total idiot for trying to
hide it with my Voice Change skill!

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:43.790
Are you really the Superior Killer, Marie?

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:48.500
This is kind of an emergency,
so how about we save that for later?

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.410
Sure. But you owe me a duel, all right?

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:55.040
Understood. And I won't hold back!

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.580
Okay, so that's <i>two</i> .

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:04.250
There's no way in hell two measly Masters
can stop 5,000 modded monsters!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:09.160
Then we'll stop them with 20!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.200
Rook!

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.120
Ray! Ma--

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:16.370
...MacBlackmist! I've brought backup!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:19.450
MacBlackmist? Is that supposed to be <i>me</i> ?!

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.700
Ridiculous.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:28.370
A bunch of rookies.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:32.200
Plus high-rank Masters
who ought to be Frozen solid.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:37.040
Even if Yu ate the penalty for dying,
that Frozen would stay active for an hour.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.200
Unless...

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:42.450
Yu... you canceled it?

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.370
I guess I betrayed her first.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:52.120
No matter! There are more of you,
sure, but still only 22.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:58.410
It'll take all you've got just to <i>try</i>
and stop this surge of magic beasts!

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:01.000
Dammit! We can't break through!

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.830
I'll let you handle this.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:26.200
If the one down below or the two in the
stands try to start anything, stop them.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.450
What about you?

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:33.160
I'll bind the possibility that he's seized.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.080
They're holding out, all right.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.450
Well, then...

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.580
Well, well.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.660
Well, well, well.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.120
This really grinds my gears...

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.540
...so I think I'll just kill 'em!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.700
DGP!

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.700
Don't let it get away!

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.040
Chew on <i>this</i> !

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.870
Huh?!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.660
Trishula!

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.660
Charybdis!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.750
Grootslang!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.000
Dammit!

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.660
A Dragon King Aura!

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:28.250
Looks like there's some Dragon
King parts in there somewhere.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.410
The longer we hesitate, the worse this will get.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.160
Arc-en-Cie--

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.580
Ray!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:50.580
Ray!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.500
Nemesis... I'm probably going to die here.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.700
But I'm not about to go out without a fight!

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:02.910
The second that thing attacks,
I'm throwing a counter back in its face!

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:04.750
Bring it on!

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:26.790
Save that gamble for somewhere cooler, grizz.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:32.330
That kind of counter is for when you know
you can kill the enemy <i>and</i> stay alive.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:36.250
If you're gonna die either way and the other
guy gets away with a few scratches?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:38.250
Pretty weak stuff, grizz.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.540
Heh. Guess I can drop that "grizz" stuff.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.540
Seriously?

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:02.250
You went hog wild, as expected.
But at least you waited for me--alive.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.080
You came.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.330
I told you I'd be right there.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:13.290
Hello? Testing, testing!
Can you hear me, Franklin?

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.790
Yeah, I can hear you.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:20.160
Okay, great. Now for my proclamation.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.830
Your proclamation?

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:27.370
You made a huge mistake in your game tonight:

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:31.160
Antagonizing me and my little bro here.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.620
And now the King of Destruction

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:38.910
will obliterate every last one
of your precious monsters!

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:53.000
You've got to be kidding me.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:56.500
Those are Superior-equivalent
Demi-Drag-class monsters,

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.950
and he's blowing through them
like so much paper.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.040
This is awful.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:11.830
The King of Destruction's job level alone
is 1,080--and his STR is over 100,000!

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:17.250
He might just be the mightiest
Master around on STR alone.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.870
But that's all.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:22.870
He's put everything into his STR stat,
but his AGI is barely cracking four digits.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.080
And yet...

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.370
It just doesn't make sense.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:33.410
How can monsters made for speed
not be able to land even a single blow?

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:37.660
Don't tell me it's a boost
from his IRL martial arts.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:42.500
"If your foe is ten times faster,
just read ten moves ahead."

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:44.200
What's that supposed to mean?

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.660
Apparently, he's predicting the enemy's moves

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:52.750
and placing attacks at points where
they can't alter their trajectory.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:57.000
That bear--he deflected my attacks, too.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:02.330
Still, reading ten moves ahead?
Who can even <i>do</i> that?

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.410
Well, <i>he</i> can.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.620
He dabbled in martial arts back in the day.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.040
Wow! Martial arts, huh?

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:16.330
Wait, wasn't he wearing a bear costume?
What's with <i>that</i> getup?

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.000
Still bearish, I guess.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:23.200
That's a convertible piece
of gear: Mythical Godcloth.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.830
By the way...

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.080
Yes?

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:31.120
When will that lab-coated loser
trigger the thing under us?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.660
It's probably a tactical self-destruct monster--

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.910
I'm thinking he'll use it
after his Plan C fails.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.450
And that'll be soon enough.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:44.950
All right: I'll finish it off
with my ultimate skill.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.620
And you...

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:52.080
I'll stop the two strongest in the stands
if either one goes on the offensive.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.700
That'll be way trickier!

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:58.000
Fun, though, right?

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.870
Amen to that.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:06.410
He's strong. He's using little tricks, too,
but it's mostly brute strength.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.790
I like that.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:11.540
I want him to hit me, and I'd love to crush him.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:15.120
He's like a hero.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:17.950
That's right.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:23.330
Hey, who's stronger:
The Queen of Monsters or the hero?

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.120
We'll have to find out.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.280
"Right of Destruction"
"Destroy indestructible targets
 whose endurance is lower 
than the user's attack power."

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:43.700
I've studied the King of
Destruction's skills and stats.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:47.700
They were truly surprising...
but not a problem in the slightest.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:52.450
As great as his strength may be,
it's still only <i>individual</i> strength.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:59.120
The next 50,000 Suicide Series monsters
I unleash will spread out and invade Gideon.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:02.410
The city could probably handle
a single group of invaders;

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:07.250
with monsters invading from every direction,
they'll be outnumbered and helpless.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:12.080
Some percentage of those
monsters <i>will</i> get inside.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:15.750
Let the march on Gideon beg--

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:20.750
Artillery fire? What the--?

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.830
A... A battleship!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:40.290
Twin Quintuple Cannons, firebombs loaded.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.830
Barrage.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:46.660
Stardust Genocider.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:55.290
Bloody Laser Storm.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.410
That's...

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:08.290
...a wide-scale extermination type?!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.870
I guess... this is it.

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:26.370
Plan A was foiled by Ray Starling,

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:30.080
Plan B by the Superior Killer.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:37.750
And Plan C, which took the longest to prepare,
is getting crushed by the King of Destruction.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:45.700
I whip up a better plan,
they whip out bigger guns. Every time.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.540
You gotta laugh.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:57.000
Enough. There's no way I'll win.
I know that much.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:04.330
So I'll just delete your victory--and my defeat.

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:48.400
"Those Who Bind the Possibilities"

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:48.370
"Those Who Bind the Possibilities."
